  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Cole didn't give them much to worry about, but the offense did the rest.",
    "what_this_means": "They led from the third inning on, which is not always how this team works. The go-ahead run came early. A three-run burst that made Camden Yards feel small. Cole gave them exactly what was needed: one earned run over six innings, eight strikeouts, the kind of clean start that lets the lineup breathe. Spencer Jones and Luis Garc\u00eda Jr. hit home runs in the same game, which meant the Orioles were already behind by the time they mounted anything. Ryan Yarbrough closed it out clean. Three innings, no damage, four strikeouts. Which meant nobody had to hold their breath late. This was the kind of game where every piece worked at once, and that's rare enough to matter.",
    "what_to_watch": "The four-game streak is real now, not a flicker. They're back within four of the division, which means the window is still open, but windows like this don't stay open forever. This is a team that wins when the pitching is sharp and the bats show up in the same game. It's not complicated, but it's not automatic either. The formula held tonight. The formula doesn't always hold.",
